  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has thick, leathery leaves that provide a great opportunity to discuss leaf texture and water conservation. The leaves are evergreen, making it useful for lessons on different leaf life cycles. Its acorns can be used to teach about seed dispersal and the importance of native wildlife. The tree&#x27;s ability to thrive in various soil types can also be a point of interest for discussions on plant adaptability.",
